... claim'","ABSENCE: the plan never states whether 'dirty gating' reproduces current write-avoidance or introduces a new save-boundary skip, nor at what granularity a 'unit of work' is defined given retire writes two files (retired then bindings, L612/L619)"],"finding":"Step 2's 'dirty gating' and AC-2 ('An unchanged unit of work performs no replacement') describe a behavior the code being extracted does not currently exhibit: BindingStore.save() writes bindings.json unconditionally (tempfile + os.replace every call, L282-304); the only existing no-churn behavior lives in individual callers (e.g. record_comment_id returns before save() on an identical re-record, L502). Introducing save-boundary dirty gating is a NEW invariant that sits in tension with the Outcome's promise to retain 'exact serialization behavior' with 'no facade cutover' and step 4's 'no eager rewrite' — the plan does not reconcile whether it is characterizing existing behavior or adding it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1c90f9f79d9adcd3","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 2 / step 4; Acceptance Criteria line 2 ('An unchanged unit of work performs no replacement')","norm_id":"nf7c4ef5f6be47ecf","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A save() with no in-memory mutation: legacy behavior rewrites the file (new bytes/mtime); the new dirty-gated repository must skip it to satisfy AC-2 — a divergence a byte-preserving extraction should call out","A retire() spans two writes (retired file then bindings via save()); 'unit of work performs no replacement' is ambiguous about which file(s) the no-replacement guarantee covers"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_